   "source": [
    "# Lab 2: Vector Search with ChromaDB\n",
    "\n",
    "**Level:** Basic | **Duration:** ~30 minutes\n",
    "\n",
    "## What You'll Learn\n",
    "- How to create and manage a vector store with ChromaDB\n",
    "- How to add documents with metadata to a collection\n",
    "- How semantic search differs from keyword search\n",
    "- How to use metadata filters to narrow search results\n",
    "- How to interpret distance scores in search results\n",
    "\n",
    "## Why This Matters\n",
    "Vector databases are the backbone of RAG. You need a fast, reliable way to store embeddings and retrieve the most relevant chunks. ChromaDB is a lightweight, in-memory option perfect for prototyping."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Setup"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "!pip install -q chromadb sentence-transformers"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "os.environ[\"GROQ_API_KEY\"] = \"your-groq-key-here\"\n",
    "\n",
    "import chromadb\n",
    "from sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer\n",
    "\n",
    "embedding_model = SentenceTransformer("all-MiniLM-L6-v2")\n",
    "chroma_client = chromadb.Client()\n",
    "print(\"Setup complete!\")"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 1: Prepare Sample Documents\n",
    "\n",
    "We'll use travel and aviation-related documents. Each document has content and metadata (category, source, date)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "documents = [\n    {\n        \"id\": \"doc1\",\n        \"text\": \"Passengers can check in online starting 24 hours before departure. Online check-in is available for all flights except those departing from airports with special security requirements.\",\n        \"metadata\": {\"category\": \"check-in\", \"source\": \"operations-manual\", \"year\": 2024}\n    },\n    {\n        \"id\": \"doc2\",\n        \"text\": \"Economy class passengers are allowed one carry-on bag (max 8kg) and one personal item. Business class passengers may carry two carry-on bags (max 8kg each) plus one personal item.\",\n        \"metadata\": {\"category\": \"baggage\", \"source\": \"passenger-guide\", \"year\": 2024}\n    },\n    {\n        \"id\": \"doc3\",\n        \"text\": \"Flight delays of more than 3 hours entitle passengers to compensation under EU regulation EC 261/2004. The amount ranges from 250 to 600 euros depending on flight distance.\",\n        \"metadata\": {\"category\": \"compensation\", \"source\": \"legal-guide\", \"year\": 2023}\n    },\n    {\n        \"id\": \"doc4\",\n        \"text\": \"The Altea Departure Control System (DCS) manages passenger check-in, boarding, and flight close operations. It integrates with airport systems for real-time gate management.\",\n        \"metadata\": {\"category\": \"systems\", \"source\": \"tech-docs\", \"year\": 2024}\n    },\n    {\n        \"id\": \"doc5\",\n        \"text\": \"Frequent flyer members earn miles based on the fare class and distance flown. Gold members receive priority boarding, lounge access, and an extra checked bag allowance.\",\n        \"metadata\": {\"category\": \"loyalty\", \"source\": \"loyalty-program\", \"year\": 2024}\n    },\n    {\n        \"id\": \"doc6\",\n        \"text\": \"Aircraft must undergo a C-check maintenance inspection every 18 to 24 months. This involves a thorough inspection of the aircraft structure, systems, and components, typically taking 1-2 weeks.\",\n        \"metadata\": {\"category\": \"maintenance\", \"source\": \"engineering-manual\", \"year\": 2023}\n    },\n    {\n        \"id\": \"doc7\",\n        \"text\": \"Revenue management uses demand forecasting models to optimize seat pricing. The system adjusts fares dynamically based on booking pace, seasonality, and competitive pricing.\",\n        \"metadata\": {\"category\": \"revenue\", \"source\": \"commercial-guide\", \"year\": 2024}\n    },\n    {\n        \"id\": \"doc8\",\n        \"text\": \"Boarding is conducted in zones: Zone 1 for business class and premium members, Zone 2 for emergency exit rows, Zone 3 for window seats, and Zone 4 for remaining passengers.\",\n        \"metadata\": {\"category\": \"boarding\", \"source\": \"operations-manual\", \"year\": 2024}\n    },\n    {\n        \"id\": \"doc9\",\n        \"text\": \"Overweight baggage fees apply to checked bags exceeding 23kg in economy class. The fee is 15 euros per kilogram for the first 9kg overage, and 25 euros per kilogram thereafter.\",\n        \"metadata\": {\"category\": \"baggage\", \"source\": \"passenger-guide\", \"year\": 2024}\n    },\n    {\n        \"id\": \"doc10\",\n        \"text\": \"In case of overbooking, volunteers are sought first. If insufficient volunteers, passengers are denied boarding in reverse order of check-in time, with compensation provided per EU regulations.\",\n        \"metadata\": {\"category\": \"compensation\", \"source\": \"legal-guide\", \"year\": 2023}\n    },\n]\n\nprint(f\"Prepared {len(documents)} documents.\")\nfor doc in documents[:3]:\n    print(f\"  [{doc['metadata']['category']}] {doc['text'][:60]}...\")",
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 2: Create Embeddings\n",
    "\n",
    "We'll generate embeddings for all documents using Sentence Transformers and then store them in ChromaDB."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "def get_embeddings(texts, model=\"all-MiniLM-L6-v2\"):\n",
    "    response = client.embeddings.create(input=texts, model=model)\n",
    "    return [item.embedding for item in response.data]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Generate embeddings for all documents\n",
    "doc_texts = [d[\"text\"] for d in documents]\n",
    "doc_embeddings = get_embeddings(doc_texts)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Generated {len(doc_embeddings)} embeddings, each with {len(doc_embeddings[0])} dimensions.\")"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 3: Create a ChromaDB Collection\n",
    "\n",
    "A collection is like a table in a traditional database, but optimized for vector similarity search."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Delete collection if it already exists (for re-runs)\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    chroma_client.delete_collection(\"travel_docs\")\n",
    "except:\n",
    "    pass\n",
    "\n",
    "collection = chroma_client.create_collection(\n",
    "    name=\"travel_docs\",\n",
    "    metadata={\"hnsw:space\": \"cosine\"}  # Use cosine similarity\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add documents with their embeddings and metadata\n",
    "collection.add(\n",
    "    ids=[d[\"id\"] for d in documents],\n",
    "    documents=[d[\"text\"] for d in documents],\n",
    "    embeddings=doc_embeddings,\n",
    "    metadatas=[d[\"metadata\"] for d in documents],\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Collection '{collection.name}' created with {collection.count()} documents.\")"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 4: Semantic Search\n",
    "\n",
    "Now let's query! We embed the query and find the most similar documents. Notice that it works even when the query uses different words than the documents."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "def search(query, n_results=3, where=None):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Search the collection with a natural language query.\"\"\"\n",
    "    query_embedding = get_embeddings([query])[0]\n",
    "    results = collection.query(\n",
    "        query_embeddings=[query_embedding],\n",
    "        n_results=n_results,\n",
    "        where=where,\n",
    "        include=[\"documents\", \"distances\", \"metadatas\"],\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    return results\n",
    "\n",
    "# Try a semantic query\n",
    "query = \"How much luggage can I bring on the plane?\"\n",
    "results = search(query)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Query: \\\"{query}\\\"\\n\")\n",
    "for i in range(len(results[\"ids\"][0])):\n",
    "    print(f\"Result {i+1} (distance: {results['distances'][0][i]:.4f}):\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Category: {results['metadatas'][0][i]['category']}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  {results['documents'][0][i][:100]}...\\n\")"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Notice:** The query says \"luggage\" but the documents say \"carry-on bag\" and \"checked bags.\" Semantic search handles this synonym gap naturally."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 5: Keyword Search vs Semantic Search\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's implement a simple keyword search and compare it to semantic search on the same queries."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "def keyword_search(query, documents, n_results=3):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Simple keyword search using term overlap.\"\"\"\n",
    "    query_terms = set(query.lower().split())\n",
    "    scores = []\n",
    "    for doc in documents:\n",
    "        doc_terms = set(doc[\"text\"].lower().split())\n",
    "        overlap = len(query_terms & doc_terms)\n",
    "        scores.append((overlap, doc))\n",
    "    scores.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n",
    "    return scores[:n_results]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Queries where semantic search shines\n",
    "test_queries = [\n",
    "    \"How much luggage can I bring on the plane?\",     # synonyms\n",
    "    \"What happens if my flight is very late?\",         # paraphrasing\n",
    "    \"How does the airline decide ticket prices?\",      # conceptual\n",
    "    \"I want to earn rewards for flying frequently.\",   # indirect reference\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "for query in test_queries:\n",
    "    print(f\"\\nQuery: \\\"{query}\\\"\")\n",
    "    print(\"-\" * 60)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Keyword search\n",
    "    kw_results = keyword_search(query, documents, n_results=1)\n",
    "    print(f\"Keyword search top result (overlap: {kw_results[0][0]} words):\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  [{kw_results[0][1]['metadata']['category']}] {kw_results[0][1]['text'][:80]}...\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Semantic search\n",
    "    sem_results = search(query, n_results=1)\n",
    "    print(f\"Semantic search top result (distance: {sem_results['distances'][0][0]:.4f}):\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  [{sem_results['metadatas'][0][0]['category']}] {sem_results['documents'][0][0][:80]}...\")"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 6: Metadata Filtering\n",
    "\n",
    "ChromaDB supports filtering by metadata before performing similarity search. This is crucial for scoping results."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Filter by category\n",
    "query = \"What are the rules for bags?\"\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Without filter:\")\n",
    "results = search(query, n_results=3)\n",
    "for i in range(len(results[\"ids\"][0])):\n",
    "    print(f\"  [{results['metadatas'][0][i]['category']}] {results['documents'][0][i][:80]}...\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nWith filter (category = 'baggage' only):\")\n",
    "results_filtered = search(query, n_results=3, where={\"category\": \"baggage\"})\n",
    "for i in range(len(results_filtered[\"ids\"][0])):\n",
    "    print(f\"  [{results_filtered['metadatas'][0][i]['category']}] {results_filtered['documents'][0][i][:80]}...\")"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Filter by year\n",
    "query = \"What compensation do I get?\"\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Only 2024 documents:\")\n",
    "results_2024 = search(query, n_results=3, where={\"year\": 2024})\n",
    "for i in range(len(results_2024[\"ids\"][0])):\n",
    "    print(f\"  [year={results_2024['metadatas'][0][i]['year']}] {results_2024['documents'][0][i][:80]}...\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nOnly 2023 documents:\")\n",
    "results_2023 = search(query, n_results=3, where={\"year\": 2023})\n",
    "for i in range(len(results_2023[\"ids\"][0])):\n",
    "    print(f\"  [year={results_2023['metadatas'][0][i]['year']}] {results_2023['documents'][0][i][:80]}...\")"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 7: Understanding Distance Scores\n",
    "\n",
    "ChromaDB returns distances (lower = more similar when using cosine). Let's look at the distribution."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Get all results to see score distribution\n",
    "query = \"baggage allowance for flights\"\n",
    "all_results = search(query, n_results=10)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Query: \\\"{query}\\\"\\n\")\n",
    "print(f\"{'Rank':<6} {'Distance':<12} {'Category':<15} {'Text'}\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 90)\n",
    "for i in range(len(all_results[\"ids\"][0])):\n",
    "    dist = all_results[\"distances\"][0][i]\n",
    "    cat = all_results[\"metadatas\"][0][i][\"category\"]\n",
    "    text = all_results[\"documents\"][0][i][:55]\n",
    "    marker = \" <-- relevant\" if dist < 0.5 else \"\"\n",
    "    print(f\"{i+1:<6} {dist:<12.4f} {cat:<15} {text}...{marker}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nNote: With cosine distance, < 0.5 typically indicates good relevance.\")\n",
    "print(\"You may need to tune this threshold for your specific use case.\")"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 8: Adding Documents Dynamically\n",
    "\n",
    "In a real system, you'll add documents over time. Let's add new documents and search again."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "new_docs = [\n",
    "    {\n",
    "        \"id\": \"doc11\",\n",
    "        \"text\": \"Pet transport is available on select routes. Small dogs and cats may travel in the cabin in an approved carrier. Larger animals must travel in the cargo hold with a veterinary certificate.\",\n",
    "        \"metadata\": {\"category\": \"special-services\", \"source\": \"passenger-guide\", \"year\": 2024}\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    {\n",
    "        \"id\": \"doc12\",\n",
    "        \"text\": \"Unaccompanied minors aged 5-12 can travel alone with the airline's supervision service. A fee of 50 euros applies per flight segment. The service includes escort from check-in to the receiving adult at the destination.\",\n",
    "        \"metadata\": {\"category\": \"special-services\", \"source\": \"passenger-guide\", \"year\": 2024}\n",
    "    },\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "new_texts = [d[\"text\"] for d in new_docs]\n",
    "new_embeddings = get_embeddings(new_texts)\n",
    "\n",
    "collection.add(\n",
    "    ids=[d[\"id\"] for d in new_docs],\n",
    "    documents=new_texts,\n",
    "    embeddings=new_embeddings,\n",
    "    metadatas=[d[\"metadata\"] for d in new_docs],\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Collection now has {collection.count()} documents.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Search for the new content\n",
    "results = search(\"Can I fly with my dog?\", n_results=2)\n",
    "print(f\"\\nQuery: \\\"Can I fly with my dog?\\\"\")\n",
    "for i in range(len(results[\"ids\"][0])):\n",
    "    print(f\"  [{results['metadatas'][0][i]['category']}] {results['documents'][0][i][:100]}...\")"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
