  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Key Takeaways\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **ChromaDB** is a lightweight vector database — great for prototyping and small-to-medium datasets.\n",
    "2. **Semantic search** finds relevant results even when exact keywords don't match.\n",
    "3. **Metadata filtering** lets you scope search to specific categories, dates, or sources — essential for production RAG.\n",
    "4. **Distance scores** tell you how confident you can be in each result — use them to set relevance thresholds.\n",
    "5. In production, you'd use persistent storage (Chroma's persistent client, Pinecone, Weaviate, etc.).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Next:** In Lab 3, we'll build a complete RAG pipeline that connects retrieval to an LLM for question answering."
   ]
  }
 ]
}